{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TZDoijQCr3EmMLhGkGh2be","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Python 3.15.0 final release date\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"python news october 2026\",\"url\":\"https://realpython.com/python-news-october-2026/\"},{\"title\":\"python 3150rc2\",\"url\":\"https://python.org/downloads/release/python-3150rc2\"},{\"title\":\"python 3150\",\"url\":\"https://python.org/downloads/release/python-3150/\"},{\"title\":\"Following system colour scheme Selected dark colour scheme Selected light colour scheme\",\"url\":\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0790/\"},{\"title\":\"python 3150rc3\",\"url\":\"https://www.python.org/downloads/release/python-3150rc3/\"},{\"title\":\"Following system colour scheme Selected dark colour scheme Selected light colour scheme\",\"url\":\"https://peps.python.org/790\"},{\"title\":\"ackend engineer testing Python 3.15 compatibility, package wheels, CI pipelines, and production release readiness\",\"url\":\"https://www.refontelearning.com/blog/python-3-15-compatibility-readiness\"},{\"title\":\"Following system colour scheme Selected dark colour scheme Selected light colour scheme\",\"url\":\"https://peps.python.org/0790\"},{\"title\":\"python 3150 rc2\",\"url\":\"https://blog.python.org/2026/09/python-3150-rc2/\"},{\"title\":\"Python 3.15.0 RC2 Ships as Final Preview Before October Release\",\"url\":\"https://www.warp2search.net/story/python-3150-rc2-ships-as-final-preview-before-october-release/\"}]\n\nPython 3.15.0 final was scheduled for October 9, 2026, not the originally planned October 1. The python.org 3.15.0 download page lists its release date as Oct. 9, 2026.\n\nThe delay came from a third release candidate. The original PEP 790 schedule had 3.15.0 final: Thursday, 2026-10-01. Release manager Hugo van Kemenade then shipped a surprise third release candidate for Python 3.15.0, which the python.org RC3 notes tie to last-minute lazy-import release blockers. That RC3 page also set the final release for 2026-10-09.\n\nSince today is October 17, 2026, the final release should already be out. I didn't find a source confirming the release went out exactly on schedule, so the python.org page is the authoritative check.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"07891217-2768-4466-8ffe-2ae869db2d2b","uuid":"fe5bccf3-28df-4ada-87ce-093813a7aedd","timestamp":"2026-10-17T02:45:32.848Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Python 3.15.0 final release date","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_012XqxXsFaUsQGAz72C6bpRK","content":[{"title":"python news october 2026","url":"https://realpython.com/python-news-october-2026/"},{"title":"python 3150rc2","url":"https://python.org/downloads/release/python-3150rc2"},{"title":"python 3150","url":"https://python.org/downloads/release/python-3150/"},{"title":"Following system colour scheme Selected dark colour scheme Selected light colour scheme","url":"https://peps.python.org/pep-0790/"},{"title":"python 3150rc3","url":"https://www.python.org/downloads/release/python-3150rc3/"},{"title":"Following system colour scheme Selected dark colour scheme Selected light colour scheme","url":"https://peps.python.org/790"},{"title":"ackend engineer testing Python 3.15 compatibility, package wheels, CI pipelines, and production release readiness","url":"https://www.refontelearning.com/blog/python-3-15-compatibility-readiness"},{"title":"Following system colour scheme Selected dark colour scheme Selected light colour scheme","url":"https://peps.python.org/0790"},{"title":"python 3150 rc2","url":"https://blog.python.org/2026/09/python-3150-rc2/"},{"title":"Python 3.15.0 RC2 Ships as Final Preview Before October Release","url":"https://www.warp2search.net/story/python-3150-rc2-ships-as-final-preview-before-october-release/"}]},"Python 3.15.0 final was scheduled for October 9, 2026, not the originally planned October 1. The python.org 3.15.0 download page lists its release date as Oct. 9, 2026.\n\nThe delay came from a third release candidate. The original PEP 790 schedule had 3.15.0 final: Thursday, 2026-10-01. Release manager Hugo van Kemenade then shipped a surprise third release candidate for Python 3.15.0, which the python.org RC3 notes tie to last-minute lazy-import release blockers. That RC3 page also set the final release for 2026-10-09.\n\nSince today is October 17, 2026, the final release should already be out. I didn't find a source confirming the release went out exactly on schedule, so the python.org page is the authoritative check."],"durationSeconds":4.922321774,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01TZDoijQCr3EmMLhGkGh2be","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg73Sz8ycpjxUmpSWvJEE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes, Python 3.15 should be out. The final release (3.15.0) was scheduled for **October 9, 2026**. The original schedule in PEP 790 said October 1, but a surprise third release candidate (RC3) pushed it back about a week. RC3 was needed to fix last-minute release blockers related to lazy imports.\n\nI found a python.org download page listing the Oct 9 date, but nothing that confirms the release actually shipped that day. Check the [python.org 3.15.0 page](https://python.org/downloads/release/python-3150/) if you need to be sure.\n\nSources:\n- [Python 3.15.0 (python.org)](https://python.org/downloads/release/python-3150/)\n- [Python 3.15.0rc3 (python.org)](https://www.python.org/downloads/release/python-3150rc3/)\n- [PEP 790 – Python 3.15 Release Schedule](https://peps.python.org/pep-0790/)\n- [Python 3.15.0 RC2 (Python blog)](https://blog.python.org/2026/09/python-3150-rc2/)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":915,"cache_read_input_tokens":18622,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":915},"output_tokens":362,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"07891217-2768-4466-8ffe-2ae869db2d2b","uuid":"8f73ccfb-2d30-4354-9184-e57db021178a","timestamp":"2026-10-17T02:45:35.683Z","request_id":"req_011Cg73SynA563SZk85bfTyU"}
